# tailscaled daemon environment — MANAGED BY ANSIBLE (roles/tailscale-node, HD-414).
# The Debian package ships this file with the same values; owning it here is what turns
# "it works because the package default happens to be 41641" into a declared pin — an apt
# reinstall or an operator edit must not be able to move the port back to random.
#
# Why the pin matters: the unit's ExecStart ends in `--port=${PORT}`, and tailscaled
# silently falls back to an ephemeral port when its preferred one is busy. HD-414's
# scoped IPv6 posture is "no inbound listener except the one UDP port the router may
# accept", and a rule naming 41641 is only worth writing while the daemon is bound to it.
#
# Remote nodes are informed of the new port automatically; nothing else reads this file.
PORT="{{ tailscale_node_port }}"

# Extra flags for tailscaled. Empty by design: every join-scope decision this node makes
# lives in the `tailscale up` flags in tasks/main.yml (no routes, no exit node, no SSH,
# no DNS takeover) and a flag smuggled in here would bypass them.
FLAGS=""
